<main id="main" data-pagefind-body><section class="reference-intro"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/index.html">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Reading preferences &amp; privacy</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">YOUR PLACE IN THE JOURNAL</p><h1>Your reading.<br><em>Your choices.</em></h1><p>The website’s reading features work without an account.</p></section><div class="section editorial-standards"><section><h2>Saved in your browser</h2><div><p>Theme, reading size, saved stories, bookmarks and completion are stored in this browser where storage is available. They do not automatically sync to another device. Clearing browser storage can remove them.</p><p>The <a href="/reading-library.html">reading library</a> lets you export a backup, merge one from another browser, or clear your reading history. A backup may reveal the pages you have read; keep it somewhere you are comfortable storing that information.</p></div></section><section><h2>Site analytics</h2><p>Google Analytics helps us understand visits and which pages readers use. When a page loads, your browser may send page, device and network information to Google and may store analytics identifiers in your browser. The site does not use this information to create a Sanatan Heritage account.</p></section><section><h2>Optional listening</h2><p>Read-aloud uses your browser’s speech service after you press Play. Voices and pronunciation vary. Depending on your browser and selected voice, speech may be processed by its provider. The written story remains available throughout.</p></section><section><h2>Contact</h2><p>The <a href="/contact.html">contact page</a> prepares an email in your own email app. It does not submit a form to a website inbox. Email is sent only when you send it from that app.</p></section><section><h2>Hosting and external links</h2><p>Your browser requests pages, fonts, images and video from the website’s host. Hosting providers may process request information as part of delivering the site. Source links lead to other websites with their own policies.</p></section></div></main>
